experience.description:
Applying and leveraging my experience as a practicing business coach to the Shirlaws coaching team throughout the UK and connected globally.

Responsible for ensuring our teams achieved their commercial and cultural outcomes, sooner. Primary focus was taking the strategic direction of our Board and (excellent) CEO and evolving it into specific actions that could be implemented by me or our national team.

Initially solely the marketing role, in 16 months I:
Launched our national newsletter, and grew our database by 500%;
Re-designed the national website and its traffic generation strategy;
Was responsible for our social media presence, incorporating LinkedIn, Twitter, and Facebook;
Designed and delivered a series of training programs, in person and online, as a guide to building an individual and team coaching practice;
Promoted two CEO ebooks, and published 'More money, More time, Less stress' in paperback and Kindle;
Designed, launched and evolved an Online Diagnostic Tool for CEOs and entrepreneurs, to engage Shirlaws' target clients with our brand and message;
Produced a series of reports, webinars, and PR campaigns to support the Stages diagnostic tool, and the hundreds of business owners who completed it;
Liaised with business partners in London and across the UK to leverage our reach in spreading a consistent, supportive message about entrepreneurial investment in a double dip recession.

At the start of 2012 I assumed the full COO role, which involved:
Creating and chairing the Team Leaders Forum, bringing together the leaders within our UK operations for monthly group calls and ongoing project work;
Training both new and experienced coaches, most notably designing and primarily delivering our Orientation course;
Contributing to our new coach advocate programme;
Improving communication and leverage of newly developed processes upwards to Shirlaws' global partner NavitasIP, and sideways to our global companies, in particular the USA.
